{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment is completed (config_001: RNA-only, singleprofile, PCA → 48.5% acc), which is near chance-level and tells us little about whether the image modality is informative or whether the low score is due to the encoder/modality choice. Uncertainty: The single most important open question for a multimodal study is whether the image channel carries complementary signal; without an image-only baseline, any future multimodal result cannot be decomposed into 'image contribution' vs. 'fusion synergy.' What this tests: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, ResNet-50) is the cleanest single-axis comparison to config_001—same profile setting, same simplicity (no aggregation/fusion), but a different modality and a standard pretrained encoder. Why it is the best next experiment: It reduces the largest uncertainty (modality value) with a directly interpretable A/B comparison, establishes the image-only baseline needed to contextualize all subsequent multimodal runs, and uses a well-understood encoder (ResNet-50) so that any performance difference is attributable to the modality rather than encoder idiosyncrasy. Under a tight budget, knowing whether image features are useful at all before investing in fusion-strategy experiments is the highest-information-per-experiment choice."
}

